--TEST--
`$uri->withQueryParameter` sets, replaces and removes one pair while every other one is carried over — `rule:core-classes/uri-removable-components`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Uri::withQueryParameter
// The rule's second level, write half. The member composes `parseQuery`, the
// edit and `buildQuery`, so there is no second canonicalization of a query
// string to drift from the one `Core\Uri::buildQuery` already is.
var $u = Core\Uri::parse("https://example.com/a?x=1&y=two#top");

// A pair that is not there is added, and nothing else moves — not the other
// pairs, not the fragment, not the authority.
echo $u->withQueryParameter("z", "3")->toString(), "\n";

// Replacing is the same call with a name that is already there, and the pair
// keeps its position rather than moving to the end.
echo $u->withQueryParameter("x", "9")->toString(), "\n";

// `null` removes it — the one thing a written `null` means wherever a `Core`
// member admits one (`rule:core-api/a-written-null-removes`).
echo $u->withQueryParameter("x", null)->toString(), "\n";

// Removing the last pair leaves no query at all rather than a bare `?`: a `?`
// with nothing after it is an *empty* query, which is a different thing.
echo Core\Uri::parse("https://example.com/a?only=1")->withQueryParameter("only", null)->toString(), "\n";

// A URI with no query gains one, and removing from one is the identity.
echo Core\Uri::parse("https://example.com/a")->withQueryParameter("x", "1")->toString(), "\n";
echo Core\Uri::parse("https://example.com/a")->withQueryParameter("x", null)->toString(), "\n";

// The bracket convention comes from the **value**, never from the name, which
// is what makes the pair a round trip through `queryParameter`.
var $nested = $u->withQueryParameter("a", ["b" => "c"]);
echo $nested->toString(), "\n";
array<mixed> $back = $nested->queryParameter("a") as array<mixed>;
echo $back["b"] as bytes as string, "\n";

// Every answer above is a fresh `Uri`; the receiver is untouched by all of it.
echo $u->toString(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
https://example.com/a?x=1&y=two&z=3#top
https://example.com/a?x=9&y=two#top
https://example.com/a?y=two#top
https://example.com/a
https://example.com/a?x=1
https://example.com/a
https://example.com/a?x=1&y=two&a%5Bb%5D=c#top
c
https://example.com/a?x=1&y=two#top
